walter yeah i'm listening margie only uh make a snappy will you he's on crutches the doctor says

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:01.840
he can go if he's careful the change will do him good.

00:45:02.490 --> 00:45:04.850
It's wonderful, Walter, just the way you wanted it on a train.

00:45:05.390 --> 00:45:07.490
Only with the crutches, it makes it much better, doesn't it?

00:45:08.120 --> 00:45:10.530
Yeah. Yeah, that's 100% better.

00:45:12.190 --> 00:45:12.870
Pull the line of mine, will you?

00:45:13.630 --> 00:45:15.040
Key, suppose I join you in your office.

00:45:15.260 --> 00:45:17.460
That's all right. I'll wait. Only tell her not to take all day.

00:45:20.210 --> 00:45:21.630
Go ahead.

00:45:22.230 --> 00:45:24.310
It's the 1015 from Glendale. I'm driving him.

00:45:25.100 --> 00:45:26.640
It's still the same dark street, isn't it?

00:45:26.940 --> 00:45:28.600
And the signal is three honks on the horn.

00:45:29.470 --> 00:45:30.000
Okay, anything?

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:38.580
else? No. Oh, what color did you pick? Blue, navy blue. And the cast is on his left leg.

00:45:39.890 --> 00:45:45.850
Now, that suits me fine. This is it, Walter. I'm shaking like a leaf, but it's straight down the

00:45:45.850 --> 00:45:54.760
line for both of us. I love you, Walter. Goodbye. Sorry, Keyes. What's the matter? Name's Chessing

00:45:54.760 --> 00:46:00.000
again or still? This is none of my business. If I told you it was a customer... Margie. I bet she drinks from the bar.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:02.950
Why don't you settle down and get married, Walter?

00:46:02.950 --> 00:46:06.920
- Why don't you, for instance? - Almost did once. Long time ago.

00:46:07.000 --> 00:46:08.880
Now, look, Keys, I've got a call on a prospect.

00:46:08.960 --> 00:46:11.330
Even now the church picked out, the dame and I.

00:46:11.410 --> 00:46:13.600
She had a white satin dress with flounces on it.

00:46:13.790 --> 00:46:16.280
I was on my way to the jewelry store to buy the ring.

00:46:16.740 --> 00:46:19.430
And then suddenly, that little man in here started working on me.

00:46:19.510 --> 00:46:24.110
- So you went back and had her investigated? - Yeah, the stuff that came out.

00:46:24.600 --> 00:46:26.840
She'd been dyeing her hair ever since she was 16.

00:46:26.940 --> 00:46:30.000
There was a manic-depressive in the family on her mother's side.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:33.320
She already had one husband. He was a professional pool player in Baltimore.

00:46:33.390 --> 00:46:35.380
- And as for her brother... - I get the general idea.

00:46:35.470 --> 00:46:37.460
